A||||2||pontiacs4me||difference between 1 and 2 core radiators?||||1||
Z||000000||pontiacs4me||03-10-2001||03:36 AM||||Ok, you all have probably heard of my 2 fieros to 1 project by now.  I kept the radiator out of the 6 cylinder car, because I have heard that they are a 2 core where the 4 cylinder radiators are only 1 core.  How do I tell the difference?  I thought to look down into the filler cap hole and count the horizontal fin tubes.  Is this right?  I think they are both 1 core radiators.  thanks for any help in advance.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Archie||03-10-2001||11:45 AM||||Actually both of those radiators are ONE core. The 6 cylinder Radiator just has a little bit wider core.<P>Here is a picc. of (from left to right) the 4 cyl. rad., the 6 cyl. rad & the 4 core radiator that I have custom made for the Fiero.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-680s.jpg"> <P>The 4 cyl. Rad. is just less than 1" wide<BR>The 6 cyl. Rad. is almost 1-3/8" wide<BR>The 8 cyl. Rad. is just over 2-1/8" wide<P>I've never cut one apart but you can look into the rad. cap opening and see the cores.<P>Hope this helps.<P>Archie<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Archie||03-10-2001||11:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B><BR>I've never cut one apart but you can look into the rad. cap opening and see the cores.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh, what the heck!<P>I only have about 60 old Fiero radiators upstairs, so why not cut one apart to see what it looks like.<P>Here is what that 6 cyl. rad. looks like after it's meet up with my bandsaw.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-682s.jpg"> <P>Archie||||reg||1
